{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesiCMLJ2fbHVEswrc5WG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd a POST endpoint to cancel an order, which tracks order status (ACTIVE/CANCELLED) and prevents creating shipments for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n1. **Order entity** (`Order.kt:11-16`): Currently lacks a status field; needs ACTIVE/CANCELLED states added.\n2. **OrderController** (`OrderController.kt:16-46`): Has create, getById, list methods; needs cancel endpoint.\n3. **OrderRepository** (`OrderRepository.kt:11-27`): In-memory store using ConcurrentHashMap; no status filtering.\n4. **Shipment entity** (`Shipment.kt:9-14`): Already has `status` field with enum `ShipmentStatus`.\n5. **ShipmentController** (`ShipmentController.kt:20-56`): Creates shipments with CREATED status; no order validation.\n6. **ShipmentRepository** (`ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`): In-memory store; can find all shipments by orderId.\n7. **ApiExceptions** (`ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`): Defines ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409).\n8. **ErrorCode enum** (`ApiError.kt:31-37`): Currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED.\n9. **GlobalExceptionHandler** (`GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28`): Converts ApiException to error envelope.\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n1. **Error handling**: Exceptions are thrown in controllers/services, caught centrally by GlobalExceptionHandler, response includes `error.code` and `error.message`.\n2. **Status codes**: 404 for not found (ResourceNotFoundException), 409 for conflicts (ConflictException).\n3. **Testing**: Uses SpringBootTest with MockMvc, tests check both status and error.code via jsonPath.\n4. **In-memory storage**: Entities stored in ConcurrentHashMap, sorted by ID when returned as lists.\n5. **Request/Response DTOs**: CreateOrderRequest for creation, Order entity returned as response.\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: MUST add `status: OrderStatus` field and enum.\n2. **OrderController.kt**: MUST add `cancel()` endpoint; MUST modify to return Order with status.\n3. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes needed; save() already updates.\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: MUST add `findByOrderId()` to find all shipments for an order.\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: MUST validate that order exists and is not CANCELLED before creating shipment.\n6. **ApiError.kt**: MUST add error codes if needed (e.g., ORDER_CANCELLED for 409).\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: MUST add tests for cancel endpoint.\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: MUST add test for shipment creation on cancelled order.\n\n**Risks:**\n\n1. **State consistency**: If cancel is not atomic across shipments and order, a concurrent call might see partial state.\n2. **Ordering**: Changing Order to include status might break client code expecting flat fields only.\n3. **Default status for existing orders**: The ticket says \"A newly created order is `ACTIVE`\", so all new orders get that status, but reading old orders from a real DB would need a migration.\n4. **Shipment cancellation**: The ticket says \"cancels every shipment of that order that is still `CREATED`\". Need to ensure we update shipments correctly.\n\n**Open questions:**\n\n1. When cancelling an order, should cancelled shipments have their status changed to CANCELLED in the response? (The ticket says the cancel endpoint returns the order, not the shipments.)\n2. Error code for rejecting shipment creation on a cancelled order: Should this use a new error code or an existing one? The ticket says 409 but doesn't specify which code. I'll assume a new code like ORDER_CANCELLED or reuse CONFLICT with a message.\n3. Should GET /orders/{orderId} now return the status field? The ticket says \"reports it\", so yes.\n4. Retry idempotency: \"Cancelling an order that is already CANCELLED succeeds and changes nothing\" — this means the endpoint is idempotent.\n\nBased on my analysis, I'm ready to proceed to the DESIGN phase. I don't see any blocking issues, but I will clarify the error code for shipment rejection during implementation.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**:\n   - Add `enum class OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }`\n   - Add field `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` to the Order data class\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**:\n   - Inject `ShipmentRepository` in addition to `OrderRepository`\n   - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n     - Finds the order; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n     - If order is already CANCELLED, return it unchanged (idempotency)\n     - If any shipment with status CONFIRMED exists, throw ConflictException and change nothing\n     - Otherwise, cancel the order (set status to CANCELLED) and cancel all CREATED shipments\n     - Return the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**:\n   - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**:\n   - Inject `OrderRepository` to validate order before creating shipment\n   - Before creating shipment, check if order exists and is not CANCELLED; if cancelled, throw ConflictException with a new error code (e.g., ORDER_CANCELLED)\n   - If order doesn't exist, let the shipment creation proceed (per ticket: \"Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour\" — which is to allow it, since there's no validation today)\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**:\n   - Add new error code `ORDER_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**:\n   - Test: Cancel an ACTIVE order, verify it becomes CANCELLED\n   - Test: Cancel an already-CANCELLED order, verify it succeeds and changes nothing\n   - Test: Cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment, verify 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n   - Test: Cancel a non-existent order, verify 404\n   - Verify existing CREATED shipments are cancelled\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**:\n   - Test: Try to create a shipment for a CANCELLED order, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n\n1. **Use database transactions**: The ticket says preserve existing architecture (in-memory). No need for explicit transaction management if we use careful ordering of mutations (cancel order first, then cancel shipments).\n2. **Create a separate CancelOrderService**: Could separate logic, but the controller is simple enough and mirrors OrderController pattern. Keeping it in the controller is consistent with existing code.\n3. **Use a callback or event system**: Overkill for this requirement. Direct repository updates are sufficient and consistent with the existing design.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order**:\n   - Read: Order (status ACTIVE), all Shipments for that order\n   - Check: If any Shipment has status CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409, ORDER_NOT_FOUND or similar)\n   - Write: Update Order status to CANCELLED, update all Shipment with status CREATED to CANCELLED\n   - Return: Updated Order with status CANCELLED\n\n2. **Cancel CANCELLED order**:\n   - Read: Order (status CANCELLED)\n   - Return: Order unchanged (idempotent, no error)\n\n3. **Cancel non-existent order**:\n   - Read: Order (not found)\n   - Throw: ResourceNotFoundException (404, ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n\n4. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order**:\n   - Read: Order (status CANCELLED)\n   - Throw: ConflictException (409, ORDER_CANCELLED) — prevents creation\n   - No write occurs\n\n5. **Create shipment for non-existent order**:\n   - Proceed as today (no order check) — allows it\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **OrderControllerTest**:\n  - Test cancel on ACTIVE → CANCELLED: Create order, cancel, get it back and verify status=CANCELLED\n  - Test cancel on CANCELLED (idempotent): Create, cancel, cancel again, verify no error\n  - Test cancel with CONFIRMED shipment: Create order, create shipment, manually set it to CONFIRMED, cancel, verify 409 and order still ACTIVE\n  - Test cancel non-existent: Cancel O-missing, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n  - Test CREATED shipment cancellation: Create order, create 2 shipments, cancel order, verify shipment statuses changed\n\n- **ShipmentControllerTest**:\n  - Test create on CANCELLED order: Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes as designed:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":19647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":349},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6c3d9ad-24f4-4c5e-8e06-af9454202409","uuid":"80c92219-9662-4b8c-a13c-8bbb763fd7df","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:31:20.034Z","request_id":"req_011CesiCKC4NBPh5U3vJ7rwT"}
