{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesiMcRPsUngbcjk2JdqN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests passed. Now let me review the implementation:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — BUILD SUCCESS with all tests passing\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 4 existing OrderControllerTests, 5 existing ShipmentControllerTests, and 3 CustomerControllerTests pass\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** — Implemented in OrderController.cancel(), with test `cancels all CREATED shipments when cancelling an order`\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses ApiException and ErrorCode enum, handled by GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds** — Test `cancelling a CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing`; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing — Test `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment is rejected with 409 and changes nothing`; unknown order refused — Test `cancelling a non-existent order returns 404`; shipment for cancelled order refused — Test `rejects shipment creation for a cancelled order with 409`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only modified Kotlin source files, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified Order, OrderController, ShipmentController, ShipmentRepository, ApiError, and tests\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field and `OrderStatus` enum. This is necessary to track order state.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added two error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS`. Both are necessary for the new cancellation feature.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId()` method to retrieve all shipments for an order. Necessary for the cancel endpoint to find and update related shipments.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added OrderRepository injection and validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Necessary per the ticket requirement.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** — Added ShipmentRepository injection and new `cancel()` endpoint. Necessary to implement the main feature. The endpoint:\n   - Returns 404 if order not found (per requirement)\n   - Returns 200 if order already CANCELLED (idempotent per requirement)\n   - Checks for CONFIRMED shipments and returns 409 if found (per requirement)\n   - Updates order status to CANCELLED (per requirement)\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments (per requirement)\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added ShipmentRepository injection and 6 new test cases covering all scenarios in the requirements. Existing 4 tests still pass.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added OrderRepository injection, reset for both repositories, and 1 new test case. Existing 5 tests still pass.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements have been addressed and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement\n: Implement order cancellation with status tracking, preventing shipment creation for cancelled orders, with all-or-nothing atomicity for conflicts, and idempotent retries.\n\nChanged\n: 1. Order.kt — Added `status: OrderStatus` field with ACTIVE/CANCELLED enum\n2. ApiError.kt — Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` error codes\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt — Added `findByOrderId()` method to retrieve shipments for an order\n4. ShipmentController.kt — Added OrderRepository validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n5. OrderController.kt — Added cancel() endpoint with order status updates and shipment cancellation\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 6 new test cases for cancellation scenarios\n7. ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 1 new test case for rejected shipment creation\n\nTests\n: 1. Order created with ACTIVE status (baseline)\n2. Cancel ACTIVE order returns CANCELLED (core feature)\n3. Cancel ACTIVE order cancels all CREATED shipments (core feature)\n4. Cancel CANCELLED order is idempotent (retry safety)\n5. Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment is rejected 409 with all-or-nothing atomicity (conflict handling)\n6. Cancel non-existent order returns 404 (error case)\n7. Create shipment for CANCELLED order is rejected 409 (integration)\n\nVerification\n: Command: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/. Result: BUILD SUCCESS with 20 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors (10 OrderControllerTests including 6 new, 6 ShipmentControllerTests including 1 new, 1 ApplicationTest, 3 CustomerControllerTests).\n\nNot done\n: Nothing. All acceptance criteria met, all tests pass, no dependencies added, no unrelated files modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3311,"cache_read_input_tokens":34349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3311},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6c3d9ad-24f4-4c5e-8e06-af9454202409","uuid":"22d3d5dc-b016-4b01-99b5-312ad92e0bc1","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:33:15.132Z","request_id":"req_011CesiMbWL7RCtCYcQ5BEzh"}
